title: Tackle Turn Cancellation
status: draft
created: 2026-10-24
author: adrian
context: "Tackle (adrs/2026-09-17-tackle) is an ACP v1 agent harness. ACP v1 defines three inbound signals that stop an in-flight session/prompt: the session/cancel notification, the session/close request, and the protocol-level $/cancel_request notification, which the SDK records on the request's Responder before handlers run. The umbrella tackle specification already requires the behaviour — FR-003 states that session/close cancels ongoing work and releases the ownership lease — and docs/docs/dev/tackle/acp.mdx names cancelled among the turn's terminal stop reasons, but no implementation mechanism is specified.\n\nThe implementation today has none of it. There is no session/cancel handler; a prompt turn is spawned detached (so the dispatch loop stays free to route permission replies) and runs to completion; session/close closes the store row, drops grants and releases terminals without touching the running turn; and $/cancel_request is ignored. The pinned acp-tck suite records these gaps in crates/agentkit-tackle/tests/conformance/baseline.txt: ACP-CANCEL-001, ACP-CANCEL-002 and ACP-JSONRPC-007 (MANDATORY), with ACP-CLOSE-002 (CAPABILITY) failing too. A followed-on advisory gap, ACP-INIT-004 (agentInfo), was fixed separately and is not part of this ADR.\n\nThe turn's one long await is a single streamed model request (crates/agentkit-tackle/src/agent/turn.rs), so a mechanism must drop that stream promptly and then finalise the turn: persist partial output, release the lease, and answer with stopReason cancelled. The ACP SDK (agent-client-protocol 3.5.0) models cancellation cooperatively, exposing RequestCancellation with cancelled(), is_cancelled() and run_until_cancelled(); session/cancel and session/close carry a session id rather than a request id, so tackle needs its own session-to-turn index alongside the SDK's per-request marker."
problem: "An in-flight session/prompt cannot be cancelled. A client that sends session/cancel gets no response until the model stream ends on its own; session/close returns before the running turn stops; and $/cancel_request has no effect. Four acp-tck requirements fail, three of them MANDATORY, and a turn can hold its session lease and its model connection indefinitely regardless of client intent."
goals[4]:
  - Cancel an in-flight prompt turn from any of the three ACP signals, answering with stopReason cancelled
  - Route all three signals through one cancellation mechanism so their behaviour cannot drift
  - "Finalise a cancelled turn cleanly: persist partial output, release the lease, and emit no updates after the response"
  - Close the acp-tck MANDATORY gaps and tighten the committed baseline
nonGoals[5]:
  - Persisting or reconciling cancellation across process restarts; a restarted process has no in-flight turns
  - Cancelling a turn from a different connection or process than the one running it
  - A general job-control or pause/resume facility beyond stopping an in-flight turn
  - Client-side changes or a new protocol extension; this uses existing ACP v1 signals only
  - Fixing unrelated conformance gaps, including the advisory agentInfo requirement already addressed
requirements[8]{id,title,slug,description}:
  FR-001,Session Cancel,session-cancel,"A session/cancel notification addressed to a session with an in-flight prompt turn cancels that turn: it stops streaming, finalises, and the session/prompt resolves with stopReason cancelled. A session/cancel for a session with no in-flight turn is ignored, as the notification has no response."
  FR-002,Close Cancels,close-cancels,"A session/close request for a session with an in-flight prompt turn cancels that turn as if session/cancel had been sent, per the umbrella session-lifecycle requirement. The prompt resolves with stopReason cancelled and the close request still returns its normal response; the existing close behaviour (the session stays listable, grants are dropped, harness-created terminals are released) is preserved."
  FR-003,Cancel Request,cancel-request,"A $/cancel_request targeting an in-flight session/prompt produces exactly one response to that request: a schema-valid PromptResponse with stopReason cancelled, or an error with code -32800. No second response follows."
  FR-004,Partial Output Persisted,partial-output-persisted,"Assistant text already streamed before cancellation is persisted to the turn; a turn that produced no model output persists nothing extra. Cancellation ends the turn without error noise."
  FR-005,One Mechanism,one-mechanism,"session/cancel, session/close and $/cancel_request all signal the same per-turn cancellation state, so a turn cannot be cancelled by one path and left running by another."
  FR-006,No Updates After Response,no-updates-after-response,"After the cancelled session/prompt response, no further content or tool-call session/update for that session is emitted. Session-state updates allowed outside a turn (for example session_info_update and usage_update) are unaffected."
  FR-007,Cleanup On Cancel,cleanup-on-cancel,"Cancelling a turn releases its ownership lease and removes its cancellation registration, leaving the session available for a subsequent prompt."
  FR-008,Idempotent Cancellation,idempotent-cancellation,"Cancellation is idempotent and race-safe: a signal that arrives after the turn has already resolved is a no-op, and a cancellation racing turn completion yields exactly one response."
nonFunctional[4]{id,title,slug,description}:
  NFR-001,Single Primitive,single-primitive,"One cancellation primitive (a tokio-util CancellationToken) carries every signal, matching the poll-based shape the ACP SDK already exposes for RequestCancellation; no parallel ad-hoc flags."
  NFR-002,No New Dependency Tree,no-new-dependency-tree,"tokio-util is already present transitively, so adopting it enables a feature rather than adding a crate to the build graph. No other new dependency is introduced."
  NFR-003,Cooperative And Non-Blocking,cooperative-and-non-blocking,"Cancellation is cooperative: the dispatch loop never blocks on a turn, and signalling cancellation is cheap and cannot deadlock. A provider that ignores the dropped stream cannot block the connection."
  NFR-004,Offline Testability,offline-testability,"Cancellation paths are covered offline against the deterministic test model and by the in-repo golden-transcript suite."
acceptance[6]{id,title,slug,description}:
  AC-001,Cancel Conformance,cancel-conformance,"acp-tck reports ACP-CANCEL-001 and ACP-CANCEL-002 as PASS."
  AC-002,Close Conformance,close-conformance,"acp-tck reports ACP-CLOSE-002 as PASS."
  AC-003,Cancel Request Conformance,cancel-request-conformance,"acp-tck reports ACP-JSONRPC-007 as PASS and exercised rather than skipped."
  AC-004,Baseline Tightened,baseline-tightened,"crates/agentkit-tackle/tests/conformance/baseline.txt no longer lists the cancelled requirement ids, and the runner reports no drift."
  AC-005,Transcript Coverage,transcript-coverage,"The golden-transcript suite covers a cancelled turn and a close during a turn, and fails if a late update follows the response."
  AC-006,Graceful Idle Close,graceful-idle-close,"Closing or cancelling a session with no in-flight turn behaves exactly as today."
edgeCases[7]{id,title,slug,description}:
  EC-001,Cancel After Completion,cancel-after-completion,"A session/cancel that arrives after the prompt response has been sent is a no-op: no second response and no error."
  EC-002,Unknown Session,unknown-session,"session/cancel for an unknown or closed session is ignored; session/close for an unknown session keeps the existing response behaviour."
  EC-003,Idle Close,idle-close,"session/close with no in-flight turn performs the existing close path unchanged."
  EC-004,Cancel During Tool Call,cancel-during-tool-call,"Cancellation while a tool call is in flight stops the turn; an open permission request resolves reject-once per the existing permission pipeline, and the session/request_permission outcome is unchanged."
  EC-005,Connection Drops,connection-drops,"A connection dropping mid-turn drops the spawned turn task with it; there is no orphaned task and no cancellation signal is required."
  EC-006,Race With Completion,race-with-completion,"A cancellation racing the model's natural completion yields exactly one response, cancelled or end_turn, never both."
  EC-007,Nested Agent Loop,nested-agent-loop,"A cancelled turn also stops a nested agent.<actor> loop it spawned, because the nested loop runs inside the turn's own future and is dropped with it."
